  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "game-description-d3d57ee9-2457-4981-a28e-a4d2c21389c6-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "LEGO is a construction system built around reusable interlocking pieces. A set can be assembled from instructions, redesigned, or combined with other pieces to make something unrelated to the original model. This balance between a provided design and open-ended recombination supports building, storytelling, collecting, and collaborative play."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-d3d57ee9-2457-4981-a28e-a4d2c21389c6-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "The company began producing plastic building bricks in 1949, drawing on earlier interlocking-brick designs. The modern stud-and-tube coupling system followed in 1958. Those dates describe the toy system rather than the company’s founding or any one LEGO set."
    }
  ],
